Buildings multiply the city's science, gold and shields, as in Civilization III. SaveBuilding and Building get sciencePercent, taxPercent, luxuryPercent and productionPercent; City.Boost raises the beakers, taxes and luxuries left after corruption and the sliders (specialists included, Wealth not) in CurrentCommerceYieldRaw, and the useful shields left after waste in CurrentProductionYield, by the sum of the city's buildings' percentages, rounded down, and records what it added in CommerceBreakdown.fromBuildings and CorruptableValue.fromBuildings. The ruleset gives Library, University and Research Lab +50% science, Copernicus' Observatory and Newton's University +100%, Marketplace, Bank and Stock Exchange +50% tax and luxury, Factory and Manufacturing Plant +25% shields, and Wall Street the treasuryEarnsInterest flag the engine already pays (5% of the treasury, at most 50 gold). ImportCiv3 maps the BIQ's three +50% flags. The AI (ChooseProducible.ScoreBuilding) values such a building by what it would add in the city. Without this a Library, Marketplace, University, Bank or Factory cost upkeep and returned nothing. No random number is drawn; a save keeps its own buildings, so saves made before this have no multipliers.

